          "worked": "Two distinct roots require $k<5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-2&=\\pm(5-k)\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm(5-k)}{3}\\\\x&=\\frac{7-k}{3}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac{k-3}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nFor $k<5$, the larger root $\\frac{(7-k)}{3}$ is positive. The smaller root must also be positive:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{k-3}{3}&>0\\\\k&>3\\end{align*}$$\nCombining the conditions gives $3<k<5$. At $k=3$, one root is zero; at $k=5$, the roots coincide.",
