          "worked": "Two distinct roots require $k<5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3x-2&=\\pm(5-k)\\\\x&=\\frac{2\\pm(5-k)}{3}\\\\x&=\\frac{7-k}{3}\\quad\\text{or}\\quad x=\\frac{k-3}{3}\\end{align*}$$\nFor $k<5$, the larger root $\\frac{(7-k)}{3}$ is positive. The smaller root must be negative:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{k-3}{3}&<0\\\\k&<3\\end{align*}$$\nThis also satisfies $k<5$, so the required condition is $k<3$. At $k=3$, the roots are $0$ and $\\frac{4}{3}$, so this boundary is excluded.",
